Swinggo is a coin-sized sensor that clips to a golf club near the head, records the full swing on a 6-axis IMU, and hands the raw motion data to a phone for analysis.

The ML pipeline re-derives every event from the raw data and reports tempo, starting stability, and finish stability to help novice golfers swing better without investing over €5000 in optical based trackers.

*Note #1: This project is patented and final details cannot be shared at this moment.*

**Note #2** : This product was a part of the "PROOFin10" service where we work with clients to transform their ideas (..or claude chats) into actual physical products in 3 weeks with €10k of client investment. The final outputs are website, functional and scalable physical prototype, and pitch deck.
